WEBVTT

00:01:59.556 --> 00:02:03.196
It's that thing that we have in our heads
that doesn't like being underwater.

00:02:03.236 --> 00:02:05.636
So if you think about what
the deep sea represents,

00:02:05.676 --> 00:02:06.956
it's a physical,

00:02:06.956 --> 00:02:10.276
three-dimensional manifestation
of two of the things we hate the most.

00:02:10.316 --> 00:02:11.756
And we have a phrase for that.

00:02:11.756 --> 00:02:13.596
We call it the deepest, darkest fears.

00:02:13.636 --> 00:02:15.556
Because we are air-breathing mammals.

00:02:15.556 --> 00:02:19.516
So we don't really want to be underwater,
especially not super deep.

00:02:19.516 --> 00:02:23.276
And we're visually orientated
animals, we like light.

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:26.476
But 11 kilometers underwater
is something that everyone goes,

00:02:26.516 --> 00:02:28.836
"Ah, that's really deep and horrible.

00:02:28.836 --> 00:02:30.156
That's just frightening."